The SQL Bootcamp I completed provided a comprehensive exploration of SQL, covering both foundational and advanced topics. I began with key concepts such as SELECT statements, FROM clauses, and the use of DISTINCT to retrieve unique values. Progressing to data manipulation, I gained experience with filtering data using WHERE clauses and performing aggregations through functions like COUNT, SUM, and AVG. Practical exercises, such as retrieving specific customer data and analyzing film ratings, allowed me to apply these techniques in real-world scenarios. As the Bootcamp advanced, I delved into more complex topics, including joins, subqueries, and data management operations such as INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE. By the conclusion of the program, I had developed a robust understanding of SQL, equipping me with the skills to manage and analyze large datasets efficiently. This training has significantly enhanced my ability to tackle diverse data-related challenges and will be instrumental in my future data analysis projects.
